                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This dose-response has a clear methodological consequence. When applied to a production scFM trained with standard regularization on tens of millions of cells (capacity/cell  $ \\ll $ 100), loss-based MIA is expected to return chance-level AUROC even when the model has seen the test cells. Detecting distributional contamination therefore requires the orthogonal approach of Signal A. The MIA-scFM result on Geneformer V1 (null on both PBMC 3k and pancreas) is consistent with this: contamination is present (Signal A confirms it), but it does not manifest as instance memorization.",
            "block_bbox": [
                124,
                958,
                1066,
                1149
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
